#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/as-and-ref.md:6
msgid "`as_` and `_ref`: reference conversions"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/as-and-ref.md:8
msgid ""
"`as` is a prefix for methods that convert references. `ref` is a suffix (but "
"prefer `as`.)"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/as-and-ref.md:11
msgid "`as` methods borrow out the primary piece of data contained in `&self`."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/as-and-ref.md:13
msgid ""
"Most commonly return references, but can also return a custom borrowing type "
"or an unsafe pointer."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/as-and-ref.md:17
#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/as-and-ref.md:65
#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/as-and-ref.md:78
msgid "// Copyright 2025 Google LLC\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/as-and-ref.md:18
#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/as-and-ref.md:66
#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/as-and-ref.md:79
msgid "// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/as-and-ref.md:23
msgid "// Very common on container types, see how it's also on Option.\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/as-and-ref.md:29
msgid "// Slices can be empty! So this is 0 or 1 elements.\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/as-and-ref.md:34
msgid "// Covered later.\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/as-and-ref.md:41
msgid "Method that returns a borrow of the primary piece of contained data."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/as-and-ref.md:43
msgid ""
"The borrowing relationship is most often straightforward: the return value "
"is a reference that borrows `self`."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/as-and-ref.md:46
msgid "Borrowing can also be subtle, and merely implied."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/as-and-ref.md:48
msgid ""
"The returned value could be a custom borrowing type, fore example, "
"`BorrowedFd` borrows `OwnedFd` through an explicit lifetime."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/as-and-ref.md:51
msgid ""
"We cover custom borrowing types later in this deep dive, [PhantomData: "
"OwnedFd & BorrowedFd](../../../leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-"
"invariants/phantomdata-04-borrowedfd.md)."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/as-and-ref.md:54
msgid ""
"The returned value could borrow `self` only logically, for example, "
"`as_ptr()` methods return an unsafe pointer. The borrow checker does not "
"track borrowing for pointers."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/as-and-ref.md:58
msgid ""
"The type implementing an \"as\" method should contain one primary piece of "
"data that is being borrowed out."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/as-and-ref.md:61
msgid ""
"The \"as\" naming convention does not work if the data type is an aggregate "
"of many fields without an obvious primary one. Think about the call site:"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/as-and-ref.md:68
#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/as-and-ref.md:70
msgid "// OK\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/as-and-ref.md:69
msgid "// does not read right, don't use \"as_\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/naming-conventions/as-and-ref.md:73
msgid ""
"If you want to have two getters that you need to distinguish, one that "
"returns first name by value, and another one that returns it by reference, "
"use `_ref` suffix:"
msgstr ""
